	<text>
		<body>
				<pb facs='#f0001' n='1'/>
				<fw type="sig" place="top">O. Mamen.</fw><lb/>
			<div n="1">
				<head><hi rendition='#uu'>Diary in the Far East 1937</hi></head><lb/>
				<div n="2">
					<head><hi rendition='#u'>Impressions on my return and <choice><sic>a</sic><corr resp="AR"></corr></choice> general <subst><del rendition="#ow">observation</del><add place="across" hand="pencil">Condition</add></subst>s.</hi><lb/></head>
				   <p>
					On my return to <placeName>China</placeName> in <date when="1937-03">May 1937</date>,<lb/>
						after having been absent <del rendition="#s">for near</del> since <date when="1932-09">September<lb/>
							1932</date>, there were a good many changes to be found.<lb/>
				   	It was <choice><sic>regretable</sic><corr></corr></choice> that I did not get time to stop<lb/>
					off in <placeName>Manchuria</placeName> and have a look at old places<lb/>
						for I am sure I would have found many things<lb/>
					different from what I <subst><del rendition="#ow">remem</del><add place="across">know</add></subst> it. Only the<lb/>
						railwaystations with their cleanlines and<lb/>
						strict order was atleast an improvement<lb/>
						to the better.
				   </p>
				   <p>
						<date when='1937-05-15'><hi rendition="#u">May 15th</hi></date> Arriving in <placeName xml:id='Q11736'>Tientsin</placeName><lb/>
				   	I found <choice><sic>That</sic><corr resp="AR">that</corr></choice> city changed a lot. Not only are the<lb/>
						concessions, the British in particular, growing out<lb/>
						over the filled up swamps and becoming more<lb/>
						modern in the outskirts, but street regulations<lb/>
						and new, modern buildings have to a great<lb/>
				   	extent change<subst><del rendition="#ow">d</del><add place="across">t</add></subst> the face of the old town, which<lb/>
						is more roomy &amp; modern. I was too busy with<lb/>
						my friends the couple of days I spent there to<lb/>
						take any detailed inventory of the changes.<lb/>
						Arriving in old <placeName xml:id='Q956'>Peking</placeName> on <date when='1937-05-18'><subst><del rendition="#ow">the</del><add place="across">M</add></subst>ay 18th</date><lb/>
						I found that city practically unchanged. All the<lb/>
						main streets had been asphalted, which was a<lb/>
						great improvement indeed, but otherwise old<lb/>
						Peking is the same as ever, and I am glad of this.<lb/>
				   	<note place="mTop"><hi rendition='#u'>NB See Cash p. 13.</hi></note><lb/></p>
				</div>		
			</div>		
		</body>
